menu "NanoJS8 configuration"

    config NANOJS8_GPS_ENABLED
        bool "Enable GPS for automatic UTC sync (consumes UART0 console)"
        default n
        help
            Enable the u-blox MIA-M10Q GNSS receiver on the LilyGO T-Deck
            Plus for automatic UTC clock sync. The receiver is hardwired
            to GPIO 43/44 — the same pins as the default UART0 console.

            Enabling this option causes app_main, after the TX self-test
            passes, to tear down the UART0 console and reassign GPIO
            43/44 to UART1 at 38400 baud for NMEA reception. Boot-time
            log messages (everything from "ESP-ROM:..." through "TX
            encoder ready") still emit normally over the Pi /dev/serial0
            cable — only runtime log lines (heartbeat status, per-decode
            RX lines, etc.) are silenced after the handover.

            UTC sync policy: on first valid RMC sentence, immediately
            anchor the time component. Re-sync every 60 seconds
            thereafter as long as the fix remains valid. Manual UTC
            entry via SETUP row 6 still works as a bootstrap before
            GPS acquires fix; once GPS has fix, it always wins.

            For pure debugging sessions where you need the runtime
            console, leave this OFF and use SETUP row 6 to enter UTC
            manually. The two configurations are otherwise identical.

endmenu
